WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.885
AI is smart.

00:00:02.065 --> 00:00:03.831
But the way we use it?

00:00:03.926 --> 00:00:05.642
It's frustratingly dumb.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.917
It doesn't know what's new.

00:00:08.134 --> 00:00:11.088
It rewrites code that already exists.

00:00:11.191 --> 00:00:14.330
And it has trouble with long-horizon tasks.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.471
Bigger models alone won't fix this.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:22.901
Teleion Fabric is a fabric of OmniNodes that keeps evolving.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:26.480
It takes a different shape for each request.

00:00:27.356 --> 00:00:31.284
Meta's Muse models help power the fabric:

00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:37.937
they do the work, and a learned policy decides which model makes and which one checks.

00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:44.532
It runs on any model, including Meta models.

00:00:44.724 --> 00:00:51.494
It gets better at what matters: new events, code reuse, and long-term tasks.

00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:55.954
Long work becomes small Tasks in a queue.

00:00:56.418 --> 00:01:00.738
Finished work stays as Task Objects the next agent reuses.

00:01:02.541 --> 00:01:04.529
Every run is recorded.

00:01:04.821 --> 00:01:09.007
Over time, it works out the right harness, model, skills, tools

00:01:09.037 --> 00:01:14.040
and hooks for each Task, and when plain code is enough.

00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:20.291
In our testing, one repeated job used significantly fewer tokens over time.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.970
One run needed no model at all.

00:01:24.591 --> 00:01:26.197
And we measure it.

00:01:26.651 --> 00:01:32.547
Correct answers about new GitHub projects rose from 0 of 30 to 26 of 30.

00:01:33.415 --> 00:01:36.808
Lines of code written fell 16 percent.

00:01:37.449 --> 00:01:42.845
After a forced crash, work resumed with 7 model calls instead of 10.

00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:46.744
And this is running right now.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:55.975
Teleion Fabric can run almost anything, and we decided to put it to work, with Eranos.

00:01:56.424 --> 00:02:05.987
A nonprofit presses My NGO needs help, and says what it needs, in plain words.

00:02:07.002 --> 00:02:11.778
It can be a cited report, or a reusable process.

00:02:12.454 --> 00:02:20.864
Their request becomes a public page, and agents pick up the work, one small Task at a time.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:29.035
Anyone with spare AI capacity can press I want to help, and connect the agent they already use.

00:02:29.296 --> 00:02:35.482
Then a separate worker audits and approves the result, and every point links to its source.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:42.586
A person on the team decides what to use, and every finished solution joins a free library.

00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:47.215
See it at eranosforgood.org.

00:02:47.944 --> 00:02:52.252
Open one, and press Adapt it for my group.

00:02:52.744 --> 00:02:54.485
AI is smart.

00:02:54.803 --> 00:02:57.391
Now the way we use it can be smart too.

00:02:57.764 --> 00:02:59.500
Connect your agents today.

